# Contents, not the directory itself: git cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY
# is excluded, so `src/generated` alone would make the negation below silently useless.
src/generated/*
# ...except our level geometry. src/generated is ignored because the ASSET TOOLCHAIN
# regenerates it per ROMID during a build. Our level geometry lands in the same directory
# (tools/mklevel writes it there) but is a different kind of artifact: bgprocedural.c
# includes it at compile time, so an ignored copy means a clean checkout does not build.
!src/generated/*_geom.inc.c
tools/mkrom/mkrom
/.vs
CppProperties.json
.idea
cmake-build-debug
